<%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_mail_failed_intro, name: @template_name, date: format_date(@occurrence_date)) %>

<%#
  FR-43 and INV-5. There is no attachment on this path and there must never be one: a
  recipient who gets a file called .pdf that is not a PDF has been told a lie, and §7b.3
  is explicit that the error is never the document. Only the schedule's owner is mailed —
  the recipients are told nothing, because they are twenty people who can do nothing.
%>
<%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_mail_failed_recipients) %>

<%# E-26 #6: the HEADLINE is the one sentence here that is translated. `message` is
    built in `lib/` and is English in every locale, so without this a non-English owner
    read a code and a paragraph of English. Naming the origin at least tells them WHICH
    thing failed in their own language. %>
<%= reporter_diagnostic_headline(@diagnostic) %>

<%= l(:label_reporter_report_diagnostic_code) %>: <%= @diagnostic.code %>
<%= @diagnostic.message %>

<%= l(:label_reporter_report_diagnostic_correlation_id) %>: <%= @diagnostic.correlation_id %>
